t is not in the expected sequence. Let's infer from typical test cases: In the valid case, error_line should be null, valid=true, trajectory constructed. In invalid case, valid=false, error_line set to the index of the first problematic line. For b-001, lines 2 (index 2) \"Thought: invalid order\" is invalid because after Action we expect Observation, not Thought. Or maybe it's line 1? Actually line1 is Action, index1. The next line index2 is Thought, which is invalid. So error_line could be 2. The third line index3 \"Thought: answer\" is also invalid because consecutive Thought, but first error is index2. So error_line=2.\n\nSimilarly b-002 is same as b-001? Actually b-002 has same lines as b-001 (duplicate payload). So same.\n\nThus we need to implement validation logic. The types allowed: \"Thought\", \"Action\", \"Observation\", \"Final\". The sequence must follow ReAct pattern: start with Thought. Then subsequent steps must be: after Thought -> Action (or possibly Final? But in valid case b-000, after Thought we had Final directly? Actually in b-000: [\"Thought: inspect\", \"Action: lookup\", \"Observation: found\", \"Thought: answer\", \"Final: done\"]. Here after \"Thought: answer\", the next is \"Final: done\". So Final can come after a Thought without Action. So rules: \n- First line must be \"Thought\".\n- After \"Thought\", either \"Action\" or \"Final\" (if it's the end).\n- After \"Action\", must be \"Observation\".\n- After \"Observation\", must be \"Thought\".\n- After \"Final\", nothing (should be last).\n- No other transitions.\n\nAlso, after \"Final\" should be end of list.\n\nAdditionally, the line format must be exactly \"<type>: <content>\"? Possibly, but we can assume input is well-formed with that format. The content can be any string after \": \". But we need to handle lines that are not one of those types? In the fixtures, all lines start with those prefixes. But we should still check that each line matches the pattern: it starts with one of